Wanda 3.0.0 (master @ 92f7e9bdaf71): UTF-8-safe truncation + configurable search candidates

1) UTF-8-safe truncation of LLM prompt text
   generateLLMResponse() and the query handlers cut context text with substr() to a
   byte budget. If the cut lands inside a multibyte UTF-8 character (e.g. German
   umlauts), json_encode() returns false and an empty body is sent to the LLM ->
   OpenAI "HTTP 400: We could not parse the JSON body".
   - substr() -> mb_strcut( ..., 'UTF-8' ) wherever text for a prompt is truncated
   - JSON_INVALID_UTF8_SUBSTITUTE on all outgoing LLM/embedding/search payloads

2) $wgWandaSearchCandidates
   Vector and text search fetched only 5 hits from Elasticsearch and filtered them by
   $wgWandaAllowedNamespaces/read permission afterwards; if all 5 were filtered out,
   Wanda fell back to text search although better allowed pages existed.
   New setting: number of hits fetched before filtering (default 5 = unchanged).

Apply from the MediaWiki root: patch -p1 -d /var/www/html < wanda-utf8-truncation.patch

